column92:
Nodes have multiple children. In this case, you can split the <p>&#x27;s children into three: a &quot;text node&quot;; a <b> node; and another text node. You&#x27;d end up with something like this:<p><pre><code>    {
      p: [
        { text: &#x27;This is&#x27; },
        { b: { text: &#x27;bold&#x27; }},
        { text: &#x27;text.&#x27;}
      ]
    }
</code></pre>
Not that I don&#x27;t agree with you -- my suggestion is pretty messy and doesn&#x27;t even go into how we&#x27;d deal with tag attributes -- but it&#x27;s doable.
